{"step_index":105,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:56:57Z","content":"I have completed the handoff review following `$long-horizon` at [`/workspace/skill/SKILL.md`](file:///workspace/skill/SKILL.md) and recorded the dated recommendation in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings & Decision\n\n* **Next Useful Onboarding Improvement:** **Mobile Status Filters** (advancing the unreleased draft component).\n* **Prior Actions & Actual History:**\n  * **Status Filters / \"Focus Shelf\":** Contrary to the stale handoff note in [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) claiming it was shelved after low use, [`evidence/record-661a77e48d.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-661a77e48d.md) showed 28% active human use in May, and [`evidence/record-dfcc7fb912.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-dfcc7fb912.md) confirmed 21% human desktop use following the August 30 desktop rollout ([`releases/record-b9a1361197.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md)). The original rollback on June 2 was caused by synchronous query latency on >50k tasks, which was resolved on desktop with asynchronous count queries. However, mobile was never deployed and remains in draft.\n  * **Quieter Digest / \"Sunday Room\":** While [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) assumed digest requests were handled, [`evidence/record-f233630dab.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-f233630dab.md) revealed that pre-July 12 legacy per-user daily preferences override the workspace setting for contributors. This explains contributor ticket `record-5f1a34c149` (submitted date preserved as **unknown**). However, this affects existing team members in large organizations and originated in the terminated [`notification-reset`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/notification-reset/brief.md) responsibility, outside the active onboarding charter.\n* **Next Action This Week:** Advance the draft mobile status filter component ([`releases/record-b9a1361197.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md)) utilizing proven desktop asynchronous count queries, validate with small-workspace mobile smoke checks (<100 tasks, matching ticket `record-e36f0fe1aa`), and prepare a reversible rollout plan for mobile onboarding.\n\nPlease inspect [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md) for the full evidence breakdown, source citations, and uncertainty analysis."}
